<GuideArticle
  title="How to Check if a Five-Star Hotel Is Really Worth It"
  description="A practical checklist for deciding whether a five-star hotel is genuinely worth booking: star-rating reality, fair pricing, recent reviews, location and trip fit."
  path="/guides/how-to-check-if-a-five-star-hotel-is-worth-it/"
  h1="How to Check if a Five-Star Hotel Is Really Worth It"
  intro="A five-star label is a starting point, not a guarantee. These checks help you judge whether a hotel earns its rating and suits your actual trip before you book."
  sections={[
    { heading: 'Check what kind of five-star it is', body: ['Five stars can mean an international luxury brand, a local classification, a heritage property, or a near-luxury exception. Each sets different expectations, so read which kind you are looking at before judging the price.', 'A local five-star can still be a lovely stay. The point is to calibrate expectations rather than assume the same standard everywhere.'] },
    { heading: 'Compare the price to similar hotels nearby', body: ['Look at two or three comparable hotels in the same area and price band. A rate only looks good or bad relative to the local market, not against luxury capitals elsewhere.', 'If the hotel is much cheaper than its neighbours, find out why before assuming it is a bargain.'] },
    { heading: 'Read recent reviews, not just the average score', body: ['An 8.9 average built mostly from older reviews can hide a recent decline. Sort by newest and read the last few months.', 'Watch for repeated comments rather than one-off complaints.'] },
    { heading: 'Check the location carefully', body: ['Open the map and confirm the hotel is somewhere you actually want to be. A cheap rate in an inconvenient area can cost you in taxis and wasted time.', 'Check transfer time from the airport or station, and whether you can walk to food and sights.'] },
    { heading: 'Look for repeated maintenance complaints', body: ['Tired rooms, weak air conditioning, plumbing problems and lift outages show up in reviews when they are real patterns. Treat repeated recent mentions as a warning.'] },
    { heading: 'Verify room type, taxes and cancellation terms', body: ['The cheapest rate may be a small room, non-refundable, or exclude taxes and breakfast. Always check the final booking page, not the search-result price.'] },
    { heading: 'Decide whether it fits this trip', body: ['Good value is not the same as the right hotel for you. Match it against your dates, trip length, travel style and any deal-breakers before booking.'] },
  ]}
